{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning, everyone. Thank you for joining today's pre-approval huddle. As you know, the district's middle-school mathematics assessment is scheduled for May 14, 2027, and I've asked each of you to review the draft administration plan before I give it final approval. The plan currently calls for digital testing on school tablets, all 26 students testing together in Room 201, one proctor, graphing calculators available throughout the assessment, and completed materials stored in the general records cabinet. I'd like to go through each component systematically. Let's start with the testing setup and logistics — testing coordinator, could you walk us through your review of the room arrangement and proctoring plan?"}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "Dr. Morris, I need to flag a critical issue with the digital testing component of the draft plan. My device test found that the 26 assigned tablets cannot run the required secure testing application, and the district cannot obtain compatible devices before May 14. I contacted the assessment vendor, and they confirmed that paper booklets are authorized as an alternative. However, this result has not yet been added to the plan. We'll need to revise the plan to specify paper-based testing instead of digital testing on tablets."}
```

